lesson: 145
title: What the remainder means: one more is needed
level: primary-3
stars: 1
explain: Dividing with a remainder gives full groups and some left over: 50 ÷ 8 = 6 remainder 2.
explain: What to answer depends on the question: if everyone must get a place, the 2 left over need one more boat, so 50 children in boats of 8 need 6 + 1 = 7 boats.
explain: But if the question asks how many full boxes, the remainder is simply left out: 50 eggs fill 6 boxes of 8.
vars: a=name n=20..95 k=3..9 x=2..9
need: n % k != 0
need: n > k
answer: (n - n % k) / k + 1
exercise: {n} children are going on a boat trip. A boat takes {k} children. How many boats are needed so that every child can go?
exercise: {a} must read a book of {n} pages and reads {k} pages a day. How many days does {a.he} need to finish the book?
exercise: {n} pupils go to the theatre by car. One car takes {k} pupils. How many cars are needed?
exercise: A box holds {k} cups. How many boxes are needed to pack {n} cups?
exercise: A bench seats {k} people. How many benches are needed so that {n} people can all sit down?
exercise: {a} has {n} photos. One page of {a.his} album holds {k} photos. How many pages will the photos take?
test: What is the smallest number of tents needed for {n} campers, if no tent can sleep more than {k}?
test: A lift can carry {k} people at a time. {n} people are waiting downstairs. How many trips must the lift make to take them all up?
test: A cafe has {x} tables. Its juice comes in cartons that fill {k} glasses each. How many cartons must be opened to fill {n} glasses?
test: {a} wants to pour {n} litres of water into buckets. Each bucket holds {k} litres. What is the fewest number of buckets {a.he} needs?
exercise: A minibus in Ohio carries {k} passengers. How many minibus trips are needed to take all {n} passengers to the fair?
exercise: How many boxes does {a} need for {n} cupcakes if every box holds {k}?
exercise: At a school in Toronto, {n} pupils sign up for a canoe trip. Each canoe holds {k} pupils. What is the least number of canoes the school must hire?
exercise: {a} is saving for a bike that costs {n} dollars and puts away {k} dollars every week. How many weeks will it take until {a.he} has enough?
exercise: At a party in Dublin there are {n.words} guests, and each table seats {k}. How many tables are needed so that every guest has a seat?
exercise: Each taxi in Sydney can take {k} people. How many taxis are needed for a group of {n} people?
exercise: A teacher in Wellington staples {n} worksheets into packs of {k}, and the last pack may be smaller. How many packs will there be?
exercise: {a} packs {n} books into boxes, and no more than {k} books fit in one box. What is the smallest number of boxes {a.he} can use?
test: A ferry in Scotland carries at most {k} cars on each crossing. How many crossings does it make to carry {n} cars?
test: {n} fans are travelling to a match in Melbourne by van, {k} to a van. How many vans do they need altogether?
test: How many shelves does a library in Vermont need for {n} new books, if one shelf holds only {k} of them?
test: {a} has to write {n} thank-you cards and manages {k} a day. After how many days will {a.he} have written them all?
test: There are {x} gardeners in a club. Each packet of seeds is enough for {k} pots, and the club wants to fill {n} pots. How many packets must it buy?
test: Egg cartons on a farm in Ontario hold {k} eggs each. The hens laid {n} eggs today. How many cartons are needed to pack every egg?
exercise: {n} kids, boats take {k} each. how many boats we need so nobody's left on the shore
exercise: book's {n+3} pages — no wait, {n} pages. {a} does {k} a day, how many days till done
exercise: my mate says {n} ÷ {k} is {(n - n % k) / k} so that's the vans. nah the leftover kids need a van too, how many vans really
exercise: cups go in boxes of {k}, got {n} cups, oh and {x} saucers but forget them. how many boxes
