exam: It is given that a party of {n} children is to be conveyed by boat, and that no boat may carry more than {k} children. Determine the minimum number of boats requisite for the conveyance of every child.
exam: Whereas {a} is obliged to peruse a volume of {n} pages and reads no more than {k} pages per diem, ascertain the number of days required for the completion of the said volume.
exam: Ascertain the least number of containers, each of a capacity of {k} cups, that is sufficient for the packing of {n.words} cups in their entirety.
exam: A total of {n} persons are to be seated upon benches, each bench accommodating not more than {k} persons. State the minimum number of benches that must be provided in order that no person remains standing.
exercise: At Grandad's celebration of life, {n} guests need lifts home, and each car takes {k} guests. How many cars are needed so that everyone gets a lift?
exercise: The old dog crossed the rainbow bridge, and {a} gives away its {n} tins of dog food in bags of {k}. How many bags does {a.he} need to give away every tin?
test: after Nan's funeral — sorry, "celebration of life", as the vicar put it — {n} of us need taxis, {k} a taxi, nobody's walking in this bloody rain. how many taxis
